1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,940
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:03,340
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:06,040
(Episode 35)

4
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:07,280
(Hwanggeum Apparel)

5
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:13,790
Jeong Jin Sook, Jeong Jin Ju,
or something like that.

6
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:17,090
She couldn't seem to remember
the name correctly.

7
00:00:17,990 --> 00:00:19,160
"Jeon Jin Sook?"

8
00:00:20,460 --> 00:00:23,090
Is Jeon Jin Sook
someone from your company?

9
00:00:29,330 --> 00:00:30,340
Mother,

10
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:35,310
do you know why I married your son?

11
00:00:36,610 --> 00:00:37,610
What?

12
00:00:39,410 --> 00:00:42,150
I fell for him
because he's such a dutiful son.

13
00:00:42,850 --> 00:00:45,750
Seeing how he always treats you
so well...

14
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:47,120
truly warms my heart.

15
00:00:47,850 --> 00:00:51,490
Being by his side,
I learn so much from him too.

16
00:00:52,490 --> 00:00:54,690
Is that the truth?

17
00:00:55,460 --> 00:01:00,300
Did you really marry my son
just for that reason?

18
00:01:01,230 --> 00:01:03,030
Of course, Mother.

19
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:06,810
Did you think I had
some other motive?

20
00:01:07,170 --> 00:01:11,480
So you wanted to know
why I married him,

21
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:14,180
and that's why...

22
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:16,750
you had me investigated?

23
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:20,490
What?

24
00:01:21,490 --> 00:01:22,490
Honey.

25
00:01:24,490 --> 00:01:25,490
Mother.

26
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:28,160
Yes.

27
00:01:29,090 --> 00:01:30,760
I am Jeon Jin Sook.

28
00:01:33,570 --> 00:01:35,600
What are you talking about?

29
00:01:36,070 --> 00:01:37,670
What do you mean
you're Jeon Jin Sook?

30
00:01:38,270 --> 00:01:40,970
And what's this about my mother
having you investigated?

31
00:01:41,110 --> 00:01:42,340
Well, honey...

32
00:01:43,910 --> 00:01:45,840
It seems Mother...

33
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:47,250
Enough.

34
00:01:48,610 --> 00:01:51,850
Jin Hee, come into my room.

35
00:01:56,150 --> 00:01:57,190
Yes, Mother.

36
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:04,160
You can hear about it
from your wife later.

37
00:02:04,930 --> 00:02:09,700
I think I need to speak
with CEO Jeon in private.

38
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:29,950
Jeon Jin Sook?

39
00:02:30,660 --> 00:02:34,930
- Who on earth is Jeon Jin Sook?
- It's just as I said, Mother.

40
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:36,760
I am...

41
00:02:37,530 --> 00:02:42,070
that very Jeon Jin Sook
you had Dr. Ju...

42
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:44,640
look into privately.

43
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:46,300
What?

44
00:02:48,310 --> 00:02:50,580
Before I met In Sung
and joined this family,

45
00:02:51,540 --> 00:02:53,910
my former name was Jeon Jin Sook.

46
00:02:55,350 --> 00:02:59,480
I don't believe this was something
you needed to hire an outsider for.

47
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:03,590
If you have questions,
please ask me directly, Mother.

48
00:03:04,090 --> 00:03:07,690
Fine, so I looked into
my daughter-in-law.

49
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:12,660
I was curious and worried
that you might have flaws...

50
00:03:12,730 --> 00:03:14,530
as a business leader.

51
00:03:16,570 --> 00:03:19,370
Don't you have something
to confess to me?

52
00:03:19,870 --> 00:03:22,810
I understand keeping
a little pocket money on the side,

53
00:03:23,010 --> 00:03:25,310
but that slush fund of yours
keeps growing.

54
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:28,480
Where on earth
are you spending all of it?

55
00:03:30,010 --> 00:03:31,150
I'm sorry, Mother.

56
00:03:31,820 --> 00:03:33,450
Lately,
our company's sales recovery...

57
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:36,820
to pre-pandemic levels
has been slowing down,

58
00:03:37,720 --> 00:03:40,660
so I wanted to prepare
for the future, just in case.

59
00:03:41,430 --> 00:03:42,530
I'll be more careful.

60
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,230
I'll keep an eye on you.

61
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:49,700
Go get some rest.

62
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:52,870
Yes, please rest well too, Mother.

63
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:57,040
Jin Hee.

64
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:00,710
Yes, Mother?

65
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:03,620
By the way, is it true...

66
00:04:04,250 --> 00:04:08,590
that your old name
was Jeon Jin Sook?

67
00:04:09,050 --> 00:04:13,320
You brought that up
out of your own mouth, didn't you?

68
00:04:14,230 --> 00:04:18,800
I did look into
your background, sure,

69
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:23,700
but there's another woman
I'm looking for named Jeong Jin Ju.

70
00:04:24,670 --> 00:04:26,500
Hearing your name
just reminded me of hers.

71
00:04:28,110 --> 00:04:29,370
Jeong Jin Ju?

72
00:04:29,710 --> 00:04:34,180
That woman owes me
quite an old debt.

73
00:04:34,850 --> 00:04:37,720
What a wicked creature.

74
00:04:42,020 --> 00:04:43,150
Get some sleep, Mother.

75
00:05:07,280 --> 00:05:08,980
Even if you dig into me,

76
00:05:10,650 --> 00:05:14,120
you really shouldn't be curious
about my past, Mother.

77
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:20,020
Because who knows
what I might do then.

78
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:27,400
Honey.

79
00:05:27,900 --> 00:05:29,670
I was worried and about to go in.

80
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:31,100
What did Mother say?

81
00:05:31,700 --> 00:05:34,210
And what was that
about Jeon Jin Sook?

82
00:05:35,940 --> 00:05:37,140
Let's go inside first.

83
00:05:37,310 --> 00:05:39,810
I'll explain everything to you
step by step.

84
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:51,020
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine,
Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

85
00:05:57,700 --> 00:06:00,060
Why is she all alone at this hour?

86
00:06:24,820 --> 00:06:27,190
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

87
00:06:27,330 --> 00:06:28,590
Whatever medication you're on,

88
00:06:29,190 --> 00:06:31,630
you shouldn't drink while taking it.

89
00:06:32,930 --> 00:06:35,700
Gosh,
I didn't even hear you come in.

90
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:38,200
What should I do?
We're closed for the night.

91
00:06:38,900 --> 00:06:41,840
Of all nights,
we're all out of chicken, too.

92
00:06:42,170 --> 00:06:44,810
I saw you drinking alone,
so I just stepped in.

93
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:47,950
You still don't look very well.

94
00:06:51,250 --> 00:06:52,850
Have a seat.

95
00:06:53,350 --> 00:06:54,350
Thank you.

96
00:06:58,390 --> 00:07:00,460
("Don't Be Surprised!"
Plays by Kim Soon Shin)

97
00:07:01,460 --> 00:07:04,900
You must really love
that play collection, Dr. Ju.

98
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:07,600
You know how there are
books like that?

99
00:07:07,670 --> 00:07:11,140
The kind of staple book
that everyone picks up and reads...

100
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:12,700
once or twice a year?

101
00:07:14,170 --> 00:07:16,840
Back in my school days,
I loved reading books too.

102
00:07:18,010 --> 00:07:20,040
I was even in the theater club
in middle school.

103
00:07:20,310 --> 00:07:21,810
We entered contests and won awards.

104
00:07:23,350 --> 00:07:26,680
Back then, I was so sure
I'd become a stage actress.

105
00:07:28,190 --> 00:07:29,190
What about now?

106
00:07:30,290 --> 00:07:31,320
Now...

107
00:07:31,660 --> 00:07:34,290
I'm just a housewife
running a restaurant.

108
00:07:35,230 --> 00:07:38,260
I can barely remember...

109
00:07:38,760 --> 00:07:40,400
the last time
I read a book properly.

110
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:42,870
Same goes for seeing a play.

111
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:46,600
Pushing yourself too hard...

112
00:07:46,970 --> 00:07:49,910
could cause stress
that affects your health.

113
00:07:50,510 --> 00:07:53,640
Doing things you actually enjoy
once in a while...

114
00:07:53,710 --> 00:07:55,950
would be great to clear your head.

115
00:07:58,120 --> 00:08:00,320
Start living for yourself now, Mom.

116
00:08:05,490 --> 00:08:07,260
I've kept you from going home.

117
00:08:07,790 --> 00:08:10,960
- I should let you go now.
- All right.

118
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:14,230
Ms. Jo.

119
00:08:16,270 --> 00:08:19,570
If, by any chance,
you feel like going to see a play...

120
00:08:20,170 --> 00:08:21,770
even sometime down the road...

121
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:30,380
(Invitation:
The House Beyond Waiting)

122
00:08:30,510 --> 00:08:31,520
Just let me know.

123
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:35,690
Hold on, Dr. Ju.

124
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:41,860
Do you have feelings for me?

125
00:08:42,990 --> 00:08:44,000
Pardon?

126
00:08:45,260 --> 00:08:46,260
You don't, right?

127
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:51,340
It's just that from where I stand,
you're always looking out for me,

128
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:52,970
and now you're even
offering play tickets,

129
00:08:53,670 --> 00:08:55,940
so I'm a bit flustered and curious.

130
00:08:57,740 --> 00:09:00,540
I know it sounds ridiculous,
but still.

131
00:09:00,780 --> 00:09:04,180
I'm sorry
if I made you uncomfortable.

132
00:09:04,750 --> 00:09:05,750
It's just that...

133
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:08,590
the day I first came here,

134
00:09:09,190 --> 00:09:11,020
you were so kind to me,

135
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:12,890
and I've always been grateful
for that.

136
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:15,260
And since you mentioned
you liked plays...

137
00:09:16,330 --> 00:09:19,800
If you ever change your mind,
we can go see one together anytime.

138
00:09:20,300 --> 00:09:21,300
No pressure.

139
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:23,900
No pressure?

140
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:26,200
Yes, no pressure at all.

141
00:09:27,140 --> 00:09:29,010
Why couldn't we?

142
00:09:29,970 --> 00:09:30,980
Have a good evening.

143
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:33,280
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

144
00:09:43,550 --> 00:09:46,160
(Invitation:
The House Beyond Waiting)

145
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:59,370
With Da Mi leaving the house,

146
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:01,840
and what I did coming to light,

147
00:10:02,610 --> 00:10:04,940
it's a miracle Mi Mi
hasn't collapsed yet.

148
00:10:08,280 --> 00:10:09,880
I should make sure she drinks this.

149
00:10:11,050 --> 00:10:15,450
If she really collapses,
we'll be in serious trouble.

150
00:10:20,860 --> 00:10:21,860
Gosh.

151
00:10:24,630 --> 00:10:27,000
I really can't believe this.

152
00:10:27,130 --> 00:10:28,670
I had my doubts,

153
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:31,270
but Su Ah's mom actually lives here?

154
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:33,300
Man, how can someone
who only lived in apartments...

155
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:34,610
survive in a place like this?

156
00:10:38,140 --> 00:10:40,240
- What are you doing here?
- Heading to work now?

157
00:10:41,910 --> 00:10:44,150
You're on
the three-shift schedule, right?

158
00:10:44,780 --> 00:10:45,880
Why are you here?

159
00:10:46,150 --> 00:10:47,720
I didn't come to see you.

160
00:10:48,390 --> 00:10:49,990
Is Kkangda inside?

161
00:10:51,660 --> 00:10:53,860
Are you out of your mind?
Where do you think you're going?

162
00:10:54,290 --> 00:10:55,830
Didn't you say my sister was here?

163
00:10:56,360 --> 00:10:57,360
Didn't you tell me to take her back?

164
00:10:57,430 --> 00:10:59,600
Why would your sister be in my house
at this hour?

165
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:01,500
She left for work at dawn.

166
00:11:02,470 --> 00:11:03,600
Right.

167
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:06,000
Kkangda got a new job, didn't she?

168
00:11:18,750 --> 00:11:21,650
Hey, where does she work?

169
00:11:23,090 --> 00:11:24,260
Can you give me the address?

170
00:11:36,830 --> 00:11:38,000
Come out to the yard, Aunt Ri Ja.

171
00:11:41,210 --> 00:11:43,570
Did she really think she could
hold out without telling me?

172
00:11:43,910 --> 00:11:45,010
Give me a break.

173
00:11:46,010 --> 00:11:48,080
If I had chased down the money
I lent my friends...

174
00:11:48,150 --> 00:11:49,580
with this kind of persistence,

175
00:11:50,650 --> 00:11:53,650
Kim Mi Seon wouldn't have
divorced me in the first place.

176
00:11:58,790 --> 00:12:00,720
So, did you find out?

177
00:12:02,190 --> 00:12:03,190
Curious?

178
00:12:04,160 --> 00:12:07,430
Your mother is about to kick me out.
Why are you asking the obvious?

179
00:12:08,230 --> 00:12:10,630
If you're that curious,
Aunt Ri Ja...

180
00:12:11,170 --> 00:12:12,240
What?

181
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:14,270
Give me 50 dollars.

182
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:18,610
Hey, you know my monthly allowance
is only 500 dollars.

183
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:21,280
Still, at least
you don't have any debt.

184
00:12:21,580 --> 00:12:22,710
Seriously...

185
00:12:30,450 --> 00:12:31,860
That's my aunt.

186
00:12:35,430 --> 00:12:39,230
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

187
00:12:39,460 --> 00:12:40,660
Fine, say Mother is avoiding me...

188
00:12:40,660 --> 00:12:42,130
because she feels
uncomfortable around me.

189
00:12:43,370 --> 00:12:44,370
Wait.

190
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:47,540
Did Ri Ja go out
to look for Da Mi too?

191
00:12:56,410 --> 00:12:59,080
What's wrong with me?

192
00:13:01,850 --> 00:13:03,220
Hey, Mi Mi.

193
00:13:03,850 --> 00:13:05,260
You aren't even feeling well.

194
00:13:05,490 --> 00:13:06,960
Why are you cleaning
the dining area?

195
00:13:07,190 --> 00:13:08,460
I'll do it. Let me.

196
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:10,360
Jo Ri Ja.

197
00:13:11,130 --> 00:13:12,300
Yes?

198
00:13:12,630 --> 00:13:14,470
Did you forget what I told you?

199
00:13:15,030 --> 00:13:16,330
Didn't I tell you to go find Da Mi?

200
00:13:17,330 --> 00:13:19,540
- I found her.
- Really?

201
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:22,510
- Where is Da Mi?
- It's so ridiculous.

202
00:13:22,570 --> 00:13:26,210
- She was staying at Mi Seon's.
- If you knew, why are you here?

203
00:13:26,640 --> 00:13:28,680
You drove her out,
so I told you to bring her back yourself.

204
00:13:29,110 --> 00:13:33,250
Mi Mi, honestly, I'm her elder.

205
00:13:34,020 --> 00:13:35,790
It hurts my pride.

206
00:13:36,490 --> 00:13:37,990
Besides,
whenever I'm in front of her,

207
00:13:38,020 --> 00:13:39,960
you know I can't
say anything nicely.

208
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:43,090
I was afraid she'd get stubborn
and never come back,

209
00:13:43,630 --> 00:13:47,200
so I couldn't bring myself to go.
What should we do?

210
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:49,770
What else?

211
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:52,100
I have to bring my baby back
with my own two hands.

212
00:13:52,670 --> 00:13:56,270
Mi Mi.
She's probably at work right now.

213
00:13:56,910 --> 00:13:58,280
Want me to tell you
where her company is?

214
00:13:58,510 --> 00:13:59,510
Do you even have to ask?

215
00:14:00,040 --> 00:14:01,350
Text it to me right now.

216
00:14:08,190 --> 00:14:10,290
Have a safe trip, Mom.
Don't worry about the restaurant.

217
00:14:12,290 --> 00:14:14,160
Okay, now that Kkangda's been found,

218
00:14:15,060 --> 00:14:17,060
I should sell some phone holders
while Mom's away.

219
00:14:18,730 --> 00:14:21,970
- Hey, Ri Ja.
- What?

220
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:25,300
What on earth
did you actually say to Da Mi?

221
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:27,070
When?

222
00:14:27,570 --> 00:14:30,370
Right before my daughter left home.
Spill it, right now.

223
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:36,880
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

224
00:14:39,850 --> 00:14:40,850
Da Mi...

225
00:14:42,290 --> 00:14:43,990
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine,
Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

226
00:15:03,070 --> 00:15:04,070
Mom.

227
00:15:12,650 --> 00:15:13,650
Have you...

228
00:15:14,850 --> 00:15:15,850
eaten?

229
00:15:15,920 --> 00:15:18,160
Of course I did.
Look what time it is.

230
00:15:20,290 --> 00:15:22,160
How did you find out
I was working here anyway?

231
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:24,960
I was going to call you later.

232
00:15:28,370 --> 00:15:29,700
You know your aunt...

233
00:15:30,730 --> 00:15:32,540
can never keep her mouth shut.

234
00:15:35,240 --> 00:15:37,640
I'm sorry.
I apologize on her behalf.

235
00:15:40,280 --> 00:15:41,280
Come back home.

236
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:48,090
You used to tell me to move out
and go start dating.

237
00:15:48,650 --> 00:15:51,360
I take it back. Don't move out.

238
00:15:52,090 --> 00:15:54,160
Date while living at home, okay?

239
00:15:57,390 --> 00:15:58,500
I...

240
00:15:59,430 --> 00:16:00,430
Da Mi.

241
00:16:01,730 --> 00:16:03,900
I don't think
I can live without you.

242
00:16:04,400 --> 00:16:06,770
I didn't move out
because of Aunt Ri Ja, Mom.

243
00:16:08,270 --> 00:16:09,270
It's just that...

244
00:16:09,570 --> 00:16:13,840
I already knew it was time
for me to move out.

245
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:17,680
And by good luck,
I happened to find a new job.

246
00:16:18,150 --> 00:16:21,220
I thought it was truly time
to be independent,

247
00:16:21,890 --> 00:16:24,820
- so don't overthink it.
- I am your mother.

248
00:16:25,490 --> 00:16:26,920
Do you think
I can't see right through you?

249
00:16:28,330 --> 00:16:29,660
Just come home
without making excuses.

250
00:16:30,290 --> 00:16:34,030
Grandma is worried too,
and your aunt...

251
00:16:35,570 --> 00:16:37,000
will watch her tongue from now on.

252
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:40,470
I told you
it's not because of Aunt Ri Ja.

253
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:44,310
Mom, I...

254
00:16:45,210 --> 00:16:46,640
know very well...

255
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:51,350
that you raised me
with all your heart and love.

256
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:55,420
If I hadn't met you
at the Han River that day,

257
00:16:56,120 --> 00:16:58,460
the Kang Da Mi of today
wouldn't exist.

258
00:17:02,690 --> 00:17:04,090
That's why I'm truly...

259
00:17:05,430 --> 00:17:07,630
and deeply grateful to you.

260
00:17:09,070 --> 00:17:10,270
For cherishing and loving me...

261
00:17:10,970 --> 00:17:12,370
like your own daughter...

262
00:17:12,940 --> 00:17:14,970
no, even more than that.

263
00:17:15,510 --> 00:17:17,440
Why are you bringing up
the Han River?

264
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:21,550
And what do you mean,
like my own daughter?

265
00:17:24,420 --> 00:17:25,420
Da Mi.

266
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:27,150
It's true that I'm not
your biological daughter.

267
00:17:28,650 --> 00:17:31,560
No matter how hard
either of us tries,

268
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:34,930
we can't change the fact
that we met as strangers...

269
00:17:36,760 --> 00:17:38,460
before living together.

270
00:17:39,460 --> 00:17:41,430
What are you trying to say?

271
00:17:42,370 --> 00:17:43,830
I still...

272
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:46,800
loved you more...

273
00:17:47,270 --> 00:17:49,470
- because you weren't born to me...
- That's right.

274
00:17:50,110 --> 00:17:53,110
You became my shield.

275
00:17:56,610 --> 00:17:58,680
I was able to live confidently
without walking on eggshells,

276
00:17:58,980 --> 00:18:02,190
just like a real daughter
who came from your own body.

277
00:18:03,450 --> 00:18:04,490
But Mom,

278
00:18:07,260 --> 00:18:10,830
yesterday, when I ate and slept
at Mi Seon's place,

279
00:18:10,990 --> 00:18:12,930
I felt so completely at ease.

280
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:18,240
I didn't feel the need
to put on any kind of act.

281
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:20,900
It was the first time.

282
00:18:22,010 --> 00:18:23,010
I'm sorry.

283
00:18:26,880 --> 00:18:30,010
Please don't be hurt.
That's just how it felt.

284
00:18:31,150 --> 00:18:34,490
And that's an undeniable fact.

285
00:18:34,650 --> 00:18:35,850
I don't want to hear another word.

286
00:18:37,150 --> 00:18:38,160
I...

287
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:42,690
can't let you leave like this.
You must come home, you hear me?

288
00:18:44,530 --> 00:18:45,560
No.

289
00:18:49,030 --> 00:18:50,030
No?

290
00:18:51,270 --> 00:18:52,600
Let's just...

291
00:18:54,670 --> 00:18:56,170
live apart like this.

292
00:18:57,510 --> 00:18:58,740
I want to try it.

293
00:19:06,780 --> 00:19:07,890
Mom.

294
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:15,160
Fine, go ahead and live
however you want.

295
00:19:16,830 --> 00:19:17,960
Ungrateful child.

296
00:19:33,480 --> 00:19:35,350
I'm sorry, Mom.

297
00:19:52,730 --> 00:19:55,070
Hey, Mr. Debtor. Running away?

298
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:03,770
Who's running away?
Why are you here again?

299
00:20:04,510 --> 00:20:06,580
Well, just to check that
you didn't head to the Han River...

300
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:09,610
- and are still safe and sound.
- I told you.

301
00:20:10,050 --> 00:20:12,580
Over a measly 1,100,000 dollars,
I have zero intention of dying.

302
00:20:13,620 --> 00:20:16,050
All right, then tell me
your repayment plan.

303
00:20:16,420 --> 00:20:18,520
You said you'd earn the money
no matter what it took.

304
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:20,660
What are you doing? Have a seat.

305
00:20:24,930 --> 00:20:26,360
A seesaw today?

306
00:20:34,670 --> 00:20:37,010
I printed out
the repayment plan form.

307
00:20:37,510 --> 00:20:40,210
What are you doing?
You did that on purpose, didn't you?

308
00:20:40,540 --> 00:20:42,310
Fill in the monthly
repayment amount.

309
00:20:42,380 --> 00:20:43,410
Mr. Kang Dae Chi.

310
00:20:43,910 --> 00:20:46,720
Or write a pledge
on the back swearing...

311
00:20:46,950 --> 00:20:48,790
that you'll never go
to the Han River.

312
00:20:49,520 --> 00:20:51,250
I just feel so uneasy.

313
00:20:52,260 --> 00:20:54,160
I'll write the pledge first.

314
00:20:55,130 --> 00:20:56,960
You really don't trust people,
do you?

315
00:20:57,530 --> 00:20:58,530
Though,

316
00:20:59,060 --> 00:21:00,600
I guess it comes with the job.

317
00:21:10,210 --> 00:21:13,210
(Pledge)

318
00:21:27,720 --> 00:21:30,360
What are grown adults
doing on a playground?

319
00:21:33,230 --> 00:21:36,170
That guy looks just like my Dae Chi.

320
00:21:37,900 --> 00:21:38,940
It's Dae Chi.

321
00:21:39,900 --> 00:21:41,740
Wait, he's supposed to be
working from home.

322
00:21:41,810 --> 00:21:43,170
Why is he at a playground?

323
00:21:43,710 --> 00:21:45,710
Is that the girl
who came to our house that time?

324
00:21:47,310 --> 00:21:48,710
And he claimed
she was just an acquaintance.

325
00:21:48,780 --> 00:21:50,750
That little rascal.

326
00:22:03,030 --> 00:22:04,330
Mom, what is it?

327
00:22:06,600 --> 00:22:08,230
Where are you
and what are you doing right now?

328
00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:11,330
What do you mean?
I'm working in my room.

329
00:22:12,070 --> 00:22:13,800
I told you I'm working
from home today.

330
00:22:14,340 --> 00:22:16,570
Then what was
that laughing just now?

331
00:22:17,410 --> 00:22:20,040
It sounded like
a very young woman laughing.

332
00:22:20,680 --> 00:22:21,710
It's a video conference.

333
00:22:22,180 --> 00:22:24,110
Sound leaked from a coworker
next to me.

334
00:22:26,250 --> 00:22:29,120
So someone working from home
has a coworker sitting next to them.

335
00:22:29,690 --> 00:22:31,460
What a fascinating company.

336
00:22:32,390 --> 00:22:33,920
Make lots of money.

337
00:22:44,400 --> 00:22:45,470
(I, Kang Dae Chi, swear that
no matter how dire my debts are,)

338
00:22:45,540 --> 00:22:46,640
(I will never take
extreme measures...)

339
00:22:46,700 --> 00:22:47,800
(and will stay safe and alive.)

340
00:22:47,870 --> 00:22:49,840
(Product Planning Department)

341
00:22:52,880 --> 00:22:54,180
This is driving me crazy.

342
00:22:58,050 --> 00:22:59,950
(Product Planning Department)

343
00:23:00,980 --> 00:23:02,220
What's wrong, Da Mi?

344
00:23:03,220 --> 00:23:04,220
Are you crying?

345
00:23:05,260 --> 00:23:06,890
No, of course not.

346
00:23:08,560 --> 00:23:10,460
Da Mi, let's have a cup of tea.

347
00:23:20,700 --> 00:23:21,710
Was she crying?

348
00:23:23,770 --> 00:23:24,780
Why?

349
00:23:27,340 --> 00:23:28,450
Because of me?

350
00:23:45,430 --> 00:23:47,930
It's hot, so hold it carefully
by the handle.

351
00:23:50,270 --> 00:23:51,430
Thank you.

352
00:23:52,800 --> 00:23:56,210
But I'm really okay now.
And I definitely wasn't crying.

353
00:23:58,040 --> 00:23:59,410
I was just feeling a little...

354
00:24:01,380 --> 00:24:05,180
Head Designer Cha didn't scold you,
did he?

355
00:24:07,120 --> 00:24:08,120
No, he didn't.

356
00:24:08,750 --> 00:24:12,190
He hasn't chewed me out yet, really.

357
00:24:13,560 --> 00:24:16,290
I don't know what happened,

358
00:24:16,660 --> 00:24:18,600
but whenever I feel down,

359
00:24:18,730 --> 00:24:20,330
drinking something warm
and sweet like this...

360
00:24:20,400 --> 00:24:21,400
always makes me feel better.

361
00:24:22,400 --> 00:24:23,530
Thank you.

362
00:24:24,730 --> 00:24:26,340
It's been a while
since I had citron tea.

363
00:24:26,600 --> 00:24:27,600
It's delicious.

364
00:24:37,680 --> 00:24:40,620
He never treats me like that,
even though we're on the same team.

365
00:24:41,050 --> 00:24:43,090
Who is she for him
to coddle her like that?

366
00:24:51,160 --> 00:24:54,130
As soon as you see this,
get to my office right now.

367
00:24:54,830 --> 00:24:57,730
- What is it? Did something happen?
- No, it's just that...

368
00:24:57,970 --> 00:25:00,000
Head Designer Cha told me
to come in right away.

369
00:25:01,370 --> 00:25:02,940
What a terrible boss, seriously.

370
00:25:04,070 --> 00:25:07,410
Thank you, Team Leader Cha.
I really enjoyed the tea.

371
00:25:14,990 --> 00:25:16,220
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

372
00:25:19,760 --> 00:25:21,520
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

373
00:25:21,590 --> 00:25:23,530
I don't see the kids' mom anywhere.

374
00:25:24,560 --> 00:25:26,400
She's not the type
to leave the restaurant empty.

375
00:25:27,400 --> 00:25:29,400
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

376
00:25:33,100 --> 00:25:34,200
Isn't that Ye Ri's dad?

377
00:25:36,970 --> 00:25:39,080
- What are you doing here, honey?
- Ji Young.

378
00:25:43,250 --> 00:25:45,450
What are you standing
around here for?

379
00:25:46,380 --> 00:25:47,950
Well, I got worried...

380
00:25:48,290 --> 00:25:50,850
that you might have gotten
into a fight with her.

381
00:25:51,050 --> 00:25:52,190
Do I work over there?

382
00:25:52,490 --> 00:25:54,160
If you'd been worried about me,
you should've come to the clinic.

383
00:25:54,220 --> 00:25:55,660
I was just on my way.

384
00:25:57,430 --> 00:26:00,800
You look exceptionally pretty today.
Goodness.

385
00:26:00,860 --> 00:26:03,930
Please. Don't pull
that worn-out trick on me.

386
00:26:04,670 --> 00:26:06,370
Do you really think
I'll fall for that?

387
00:26:07,500 --> 00:26:09,370
No, I really mean it.

388
00:26:10,140 --> 00:26:11,510
Let me see.

389
00:26:11,980 --> 00:26:15,580
Your skin is glowing as always.

390
00:26:16,080 --> 00:26:18,050
Stop it, seriously.

391
00:26:27,160 --> 00:26:29,330
Why am I suddenly remembering this?

392
00:26:30,360 --> 00:26:32,800
Right, I mean... Okay.

393
00:26:35,570 --> 00:26:36,870
Have they lost their minds?

394
00:26:37,430 --> 00:26:39,440
Oh, no. Mi Mi! What do we do?

395
00:26:44,040 --> 00:26:45,140
Honey, you're here?

396
00:26:45,880 --> 00:26:47,180
What? Honey?

397
00:26:48,080 --> 00:26:50,650
Exactly, who are you calling honey?

398
00:26:51,580 --> 00:26:54,150
You two, whether it was
20 years ago or now,

399
00:26:54,220 --> 00:26:56,820
have consistently lacked
even an ounce of conscience.

400
00:26:57,920 --> 00:27:00,920
Fine. If awful people like you
can do whatever they want,

401
00:27:00,920 --> 00:27:02,260
why shouldn't I do the same?

402
00:27:04,060 --> 00:27:05,060
Out of my way.

403
00:27:05,960 --> 00:27:07,430
What do I do?

404
00:27:07,430 --> 00:27:09,530
I think she's going
to tell Director Ju to fire me.

405
00:27:09,530 --> 00:27:10,600
No.

406
00:27:10,670 --> 00:27:12,440
- No, Mi Mi.
- Wait, I'll come with you.

407
00:27:14,300 --> 00:27:16,240
If I go in too,
it'll just make things worse, right?

408
00:27:17,940 --> 00:27:19,610
What do I do?

409
00:27:23,510 --> 00:27:24,910
Hello, Dr. Ju.

410
00:27:26,920 --> 00:27:28,120
Ms. Jo.

411
00:27:29,790 --> 00:27:31,920
I came because I have
something urgent to tell you.

412
00:27:53,340 --> 00:27:55,180
(Mission: Mompossible)

413
00:27:55,750 --> 00:27:57,480
In Hwanggeum Apparel's brilliant progress,

414
00:27:57,580 --> 00:27:59,520
Summit Two Partners is honored
to join you.

415
00:27:59,680 --> 00:28:02,950
Who's the real owner of that
seven percent stake, Aunt Jin Hee?

416
00:28:03,250 --> 00:28:05,620
Are you going to drop
the background check?

417
00:28:05,820 --> 00:28:07,290
What will you do about Kang Da Mi?

418
00:28:07,490 --> 00:28:11,060
I hope you can handle
things like this on your own.

419
00:28:12,400 --> 00:28:14,360
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
